      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No, you should not take leftover Nitrofurantoin (Macrobid) on your own, especially when you have stage 3 kidney disease, as this medication is excreted unchanged by the kidneys and can cause serious harm if dosed incorrectly for your specific kidney function. Vitamin C is not an effective treatment for urinary tract infections, though it may slightly help prevent them. You need to contact your doctor or pharmacist immediately to get a properly dosed prescription tailored to your kidney status before taking any antibiotics.",
